{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Capture a page as a PNG via Firefox's own --headless --screenshot launcher (the same CLI path open() trusts), against a throwaway profile so it never fights the live session's profile lock. url empty = the live session's current page (read via eval location.href; err when no session). path empty = runtime/agent/screenshots/shot-<millis>.png; width/height <=0 default 1280x1024. Shoots the URL, not the live tab's pixels - equivalent in practice since goto() rebinds per navigation - so the throwaway profile carries no cookies: a logged-in page screenshots as logged-out. Returns {status, path (absolute), bytes, url, width, height}.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse flowlang::rand::rand_range;\nuse std::process::Command;","params":[{"desc":"Page to capture. Empty string means the LIVE driven tab's actual pixels (its real DOM, mutations, and login state) via drawSnapshot on the bound browsing context; errs when empty and no session is running. A non-empty URL takes the throwaway-profile CLI path (fresh anonymous load, logged-out).","name":"url","type":"String"},{"desc":"Output PNG path. Empty string defaults to runtime/agent/screenshots/shot-<millis>.png. Relative paths resolve against the instance root.","name":"path","type":"String"},{"desc":"Capture width in px; <=0 defaults to 1280. In live mode this is the top-left rect of the document captured at scale 1.","name":"width","type":"Integer"},{"desc":"Capture height in px; <=0 defaults to 1024.","name":"height","type":"Integer"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"rvuzgy1a03fb16529n1","readers":[],"time":1787776259339,"username":"system","writers":[]}